                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "While it worked, this game doesn't even have the excuse of decent puzzles or a really dumb but fun plot to get me to recommend it. The game boots up, doesn't stutter, and has puzzles, but to what end? It's just such a nothing experience. \n\nI guess it's under 5 bucks, so that might be motivation to try it, especially if you get this in a bundle with some other games you actually want, if it's on sale (I originally bought it for under a dollar, which was about right for how much I got out of it), if you need a quick influx of steam achievements, or if you're recovering from having your wisdom teeth removed, and need a game that doesn't expect much out of you, because the plot ,music, characters, and setting are cobbled together out of old refrigerator boxes and the gameplay isn't too far behind.",
